[center][size=6][b]FIND[/b][/size]
[size=4][color=#e8c882]B A S E   S T O R A G E   S E A R C H[/color][/size]

[size=3]Where did I put the Shroud Liquid? Press Shift+F and the chest lights up.[/size][/center]

[center][b]More mods by GreeneyeDS:[/b] [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/enshrouded/mods/220]The Worst Map Mod[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/enshrouded/mods/195]Quick Deposit[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/enshrouded/mods/219]Embervale Teleport[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/enshrouded/mods/255]Town Portals[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/enshrouded/mods/272]Hollow Halls Progression[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/enshrouded/mods/197]Continue[/url][/center]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/200/200-1792609966-1205231011.png[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]What it does[/b][/size]

Stand in your base and press [b]Shift+F[/b]. A search box opens, drawn with the game's own dialog, so it looks like part of Enshrouded. Type what you are looking for:
[list]
[*][b]Suggestions as you type[/b], each with how many you have and in how many chests: [i]Granite Block — 996 in 1 chest[/i].
[*][b]Pick with Tab or the arrow keys and press Enter, or click a line[/b] to find it at once. The mouse wheel scrolls long lists.
[*][b]Exact match[/b] (Ctrl+E, or Y on a controller): a checkbox in the search box. Off, a search of several words also lists names with only some of the words, lower down; on, only names that hold your whole text.
[*][b]The matching chests pulse[/b] with the game's own highlight, so you can walk straight to them.
[*][b]Open one and the items you searched for glow gold[/b] for a few seconds, every matching slot, so you see them at once in a full chest.
[/list]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/200/200-1792609967-2012517538.png[/img]

[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/200/200-1792609972-219583874.png[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]The skill tree too[/b][/size]

Open the Skills page and press [b]Shift+F[/b] (LB+X on a controller) to search the skill tree instead. Type part of a skill's name or of what it does, in your game's language: [i]heal[/i] finds every skill that heals. Categories such as [i]Guardian[/i] are listed too. The skills you find pulse gold, and a single match brings the view to it.

[line]

[size=4][b]What you can search for[/b][/size]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/200/200-1792609387-300384686.png[/img][/center]

[list]
[*][b]Items[/b], by the name the game shows. Partial words work: [i]stone[/i] finds Stone and Rough Stone Block.
[*][b]Kinds of items[/b]: categories ([i]Consumables[/i], [i]Ammunition[/i]...), rarities ([i]Uncommon[/i] to [i]Legendary[/i]), item types ([i]One-Handed Axe[/i]...) and perks ([i]Backstab Damage[/i]...). They are labelled in the list, like [i]Perk: Backstab Damage — 12 items in 3 chests[/i].
[*][b]Who can make it[/b]: the NPCs and crafting stations of your base that can make the item light up too, so [i]bandage[/i] lights your Hunter. Items no chest holds are suggested as [i]can be made here[/i], or [i]made here, not unlocked yet[/i] when you haven't unlocked the recipe.
[*][b]What stands in your base[/b]: stations, beds, torches and other things you placed light up for their own name, so [i]oven[/i] lights your ovens. Items no chest holds are suggested as [i]placed here[/i].
[*][b]Chest names you gave yourself[/b] with Rename. (The game's own "Storage Chest" titles are not searched, as every unnamed chest would match.)
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Close Enshrouded.
[*]Open the game folder (Steam: right-click Enshrouded > Manage > Browse local files).
[*]Copy everything from the zip into it, keeping the folders: [b]dbgcore.dll[/b] next to [i]enshrouded.exe[/i], and the [b]greeneye\find[/b] folder.
[*]Start the game, stand inside one of your bases and press [b]Shift+F[/b].
[/list]

[b]Install by hand:[/b] Vortex does not know the Greeneye Loader yet.

[b]Updating from 1.0.x:[/b] delete [i]wsock32.dll[/i] from the game folder. Your [i]find.ini[/i] moves to [i]greeneye\find\[/i] by itself.

[b]Uninstall:[/b] delete [i]greeneye\find[/i]; if no other Greeneye mod is left, also [i]dbgcore.dll[/i] and the [i]greeneye[/i] folder.

[line]

[size=4][b]Settings[/b][/size]

[i]greeneye\find\find.ini[/i] is written on the first start. Restart the game after changing it.
[list]
[*][b]hotkey[/b] = Shift+F, Pad:LB+X: what opens the search, for example [i]Ctrl+F[/i] or [i]F6[/i]; a controller button goes after a comma.
[*][b]glow_seconds[/b] = 180: the found chests glow at most this long (10-3600), or until your next search.
[*][b]near_meters[/b] = 2.5: coming this close to a found chest counts as reaching it (0.5-20).
[*][b]near_seconds[/b] = 3: a chest stops glowing this long after you reach or open it (0-60).
[*][b]exact_match[/b] = 0: the Exact match checkbox, saved when you switch it in the search box. [b]exact_key[/b] = Ctrl+E, Pad:Y switches it.
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Your language[/b][/size]

Find follows the language set in the game. Item, perk, category and rarity names are the game's own. Find's few texts of its own come in English, German, French, Spanish, Italian, Portuguese, Polish, Russian, Ukrainian, Japanese, Korean, Chinese and Turkish. (Corrections from native speakers are welcome.)

[line]

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Client-side only.[/b] Servers need nothing installed, and other players do not need the mod.
[*][b]Only reads your chests.[/b] It never moves, adds or removes an item.
[*][b]Plays well with other mods.[/b] It runs through the Greeneye Loader ([i]dbgcore.dll[/i], shared with Quick Deposit, Continue and Auto Loot), and where another mod such as Creative Mode hooks the same game function, Find chains onto its hook.
[*][b]Safe on game updates.[/b] Made for the current game version. After an update the mod checks that it still recognises the game; if it does not, it switches itself off (and says so in [i]find.log[/i]) instead of risking a crash.
[*]Opens only while you play or have your backpack open, never while you type in chat, rename something or write on a signpost.
[*]Works with Steam. Not tested with other store versions.
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Known limits[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Searches the chests of the base you stand in, not all your bases at once.
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Troubleshooting / bug reports[/b][/size]

If something doesn't work, please post these two files from the game folder with your report:
[list]
[*][i]greeneye\find\find.log[/i]: what Find did.
[*][i]greeneye\loader.log[/i]: what the Greeneye Loader did.
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Changelog[/b][/size]

[b]1.2.13[/b]
[list]
[*]Partial matches: a search of several words also lists names that hold only some of them, lower in the list. [i]ring mana[/i] lists the Mana rings first, then other rings.
[*]Exact match: a checkbox in the search box (Ctrl+E, or Y on a controller) lists only names that hold your whole text. Find remembers it, and the message line says how many results it hides. Rebind it with exact_key in find.ini.
[*]One click on a line in the list finds it. Tab, the arrow keys and Enter work as before.
[*]Chests and people show through walls in their real shape instead of a flat outline.
[*]The World Map's Find box (The Worst Map Mod 1.3.49) gets the Exact match checkbox too.
[*]Find keeps working when other mods (such as EML Tweaks) shift the game's internal numbering.
[/list]
Fixed:
[list]
[*]Chests sometimes didn't light up after a search.
[*]Highlights shook and slid, with doubles snapping back into place.
[*]Some recipes you had unlocked showed as "not unlocked yet", such as Coconut Milk.
[*]On screens taller than 16:9 (such as 2560x1600), clicks in the search box landed below the line you pointed at.
[/list]

[b]1.2.12[/b]
Reported bugs fixed:
[list]
[*]On the Skills page, found skills didn't pulse and a single match didn't bring the view to it after you had changed world or server in the same session. The search itself still worked.
[/list]

[b]1.2.11[/b]
[list]
[*]Find searches the skill tree too: open the Skills page and press Shift+F (LB+X on a controller), then type part of a skill's name or of what it does, in your game's language. The skills found pulse gold for 5 seconds, and a single match brings the view to it.
[*]Categories are listed as well, such as Category: Guardian (19). Finding one lights that whole part of the tree.
[*]The Skills page's tip bar shows the Find key, and Esc there closes only the search.
[/list]

[b]1.2.10[/b]
[list]
[*]The Worst Map Mod's Find box works with Find again: with Find 1.2.9 installed, its list couldn't be hovered or clicked, and Tab typed a space. Update the map to 1.3.41 as well.
[*]A search keeps glowing while the World Map or another menu is open. Opening the map for more than 2 seconds used to end it.
[/list]

[b]1.2.9[/b]
[list]
[*]Controller support: hold LB and press X to open the search; the D-pad moves through the list, A finds and B closes. With nothing typed, Up and Down list everything in the base. Tested with an emulated controller, not yet on a real pad.
[*]Every key can be rebound, and any can take a controller button: hotkey, confirm_key, close_key, next_key, previous_key, up_key and down_key in find.ini.
[*]Key and button tips use the game's own look and show your current binding: the rebound key on a keyboard, the button icon on a controller.
[/list]
Reported bugs fixed:
[list]
[*]Chests no longer showed through walls in 1.2.8: the lit chests' outlines weren't drawn. They are again.
[/list]

[b]1.2.8[/b]
[list]
[*]A game patch that only moves the game's code should no longer turn off the smooth chest outlines: they find the game's functions themselves.
[*]Find's log and the Greeneye Loader's (now 1.2.2) are written in the background, so a slow drive can't stall the game through them. This may help the freezes HadToRegister reported.
[/list]

[b]1.2.7[/b]
[list]
[*]Updated for the 4 November 2026 game patch (game build 1287369): chests glow through walls with smooth outlines again.
[*]Language: a Russian game can no longer get Ukrainian text, and Portuguese is recognised in every form.
[/list]
Reported bugs fixed:
[list]
[*]The window in Ukrainian on a game set to Russian (reported by mrniced).
[/list]

[b]1.2.6[/b]
[list]
[*]Updated for the 3 November 2026 game patch (game build 1285601). The game's text box id changed, so after a search the game stayed in typing mode: menus couldn't be backed out of (for example after talking to an NPC), and search results couldn't be clicked. Find now reads that id from the game itself, so a patch can't break this the same way again.
[*]Chests glow through walls again: the smooth silhouette drawing was off after the patch.
[*]A search closed in the same instant it opened no longer leaves the game on its hidden screen with the HUD gone.
[*][i]find.log[/i] no longer grows without end: at 10 MB it rolls over into [i]find.old.log[/i].
[/list]
Reported bugs fixed:
[list]
[*]Stuck in menus after a search (reported by bigeasier and spirevipp).
[*]No glow through walls, and search results couldn't be clicked (reported by Sh1On1).
[/list]

[b]1.2.5[/b]
[list]
[*]Updated for the 2 November 2026 game patch (game build 1283531). Find 1.2.4 did not recognise the patched game and switched itself off ("inactive" in [i]find.log[/i]), so Shift+F did nothing.
[*]Things placed in your base are found too: searching "oven" lights up the ovens standing in the base, not only the Farmer who makes them. Stations, beds, torches and the like that no chest holds are suggested as "placed here" (with how many, if more than one).
[/list]

[b]1.2.4[/b]
[list]
[*]The hotkey opens the search every time, also from a programmable keypad or mouse macro: Find caught it only while it was held, so a very short press was often missed.
[/list]
Reported bugs fixed:
[list]
[*]Shift+7 had to be pressed over and over to open the search (reported by webbj8150).
[/list]

